Tangshan, China"],"bio":{"graphic":"/mediastore/IEEE/content/freeimages/6287639/10380310/10720017/peng-3482102-small.gif","p":["Wei Peng received the B.S. degree from Hebei Medical University, in 1991, and the M.S. degree from the North China Coal Medical College, in 2005. Her current research interests include machine vision and medical image processing."]},"firstName":"Wei","lastName":"Peng","id":"570308122238781"},{"name":"Zhu Fan","affiliation":["College of Artificial Intelligence, North China University of Science and Technology, Tangshan, China","Department of Respiratory Medicine, Affiliated Hospital, North China University of Science and Technology, Tangshan, China"],"bio":{"graphic":"/mediastore/IEEE/content/freeimages/6287639/10380310/10720017/fan-3482102-small.gif","p":["Zhu Fan was born in Baishan, Jilin. She received the bachelor’s degree from the Clinical Department, North China University of Science and Technology, and the master’s degree from the Respiratory Medicine Department, Tianjin Medical University. She was with the Respiratory Medicine Ward, Affiliated Hospital, North China University of Science and Technology, for five years. Currently, she is engaged in clinical treatment and teaching in the Respiratory Medicine Department. She is proficient in the diagnosis and treatment of common respiratory diseases, frequent diseases, and critical illnesses."]},"firstName":"Zhu","lastName":"Fan","id":"38274445700"},{"name":"Zhanlin Ji","affiliation":["College of Mathematics and Computer Science, Zhejiang A&F University, Hangzhou, Zhejiang, China","Telecommunications Research Centre (TRC), University of Limerick, Limerick, Ireland"],"bio":{"graphic":"/mediastore/IEEE/content/freeimages/6287639/10380310/10720017/ji-3482102-small.gif","p":["Zhanlin Ji (Member, IEEE) received the Ph.D. degree from the University of Limerick, Ireland, in 2010. Currently, he is a Professor with Zhejiang Agriculture and Forestry University, China; and an Associate Researcher with the Telecommunications Research Centre (TRC), University of Limerick. He was a recipient of the Irish Research Council for Science, Engineering and Technology (IRCSET) Post-Graduate Research Scholarship, in 2008; and an IRC Postdoctoral Fellowship, in 2013. He has authored/co-authored more than 100 research papers in refereed journals and conferences. His research interests include the ubiquitous consumer wireless world (UCWW), Internet of Things (IoT), cloud computing, big data management, and artificial intelligence (AI)-based image processing."]},"firstName":"Zhanlin","lastName":"Ji","orcid":"0000-0003-3527-3773","id":"37577537500"},{"name":"Ivan Ganchev","affiliation":["Telecommunications Research Centre (TRC), University of Limerick, Limerick, Ireland","Faculty of Mathematics and Informatics, University of Plovdiv “Paisii Hilendarski,”, Plovdiv, Bulgaria","Institute of Mathematics and Informatics-Bulgarian Academy of Sciences, Sofia, Bulgaria"],"bio":{"graphic":"/mediastore/IEEE/content/freeimages/6287639/10380310/10720017/ganch-3482102-small.gif","p":["Ivan Ganchev (Senior Member, IEEE) received the Engineering (summa cum laude) and Ph.D. degrees from Saint-Petersburg University of Telecommunications, in 1989 and 1995, respectively. He is an International Telecommunications Union (ITU-T) Invited Expert and an Institution of Engineering and Technology (IET) Invited Lecturer, currently affiliated with the University of Limerick, Ireland, University of Plovdiv “Paisii Hilendarski,” Bulgaria, and Institute of Mathematics and Informatics−Bulagarian Aacademy of Sciences, Bulgaria. He was involved in more than 40 international and national research projects. He has served on the TPC of more than 400 prestigious international conferences/symposia/workshops and has authored/co-authored one monographic book, three textbooks, four edited books, and more than 300 research papers in refereed international journals, books, and conference proceedings. He is on the editorial board of and has served as a guest editor for multiple prestigious international journals."]},"firstName":"Ivan","lastName":"Ganchev","orcid":"0000-0003-0535-7087","id":"37267977400"}],"issn":[{"format":"Electronic ISSN","value":"2169-3536"}],"articleNumber":"10720017","mediaPath":"/mediastore/IEEE/content/media/6287639/10380310/10720017","dbTime":"2 ms","metrics":{"wosCitationCount":0,"citationCountPaper":0,"citationCountPatent":0,"totalDownloads":578},"purchaseOptions":{"showOtherFormatPricingTab":false,"showPdfFormatPricingTab":true,"pdfPricingInfoAvailable":false,"otherPricingInfoAvailable":false,"mandatoryBundle":false,"optionalBundle":false,"displayTextWhenPdfPricingNotAvailable":"The purchase and pricing options for this item are unavailable. Select items are only available as part of a subscription package. You may try again later or <a href='https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/xpl/contact' target='_blank'>contact us</a> for more information.","displayTextWhenOtherFormatPricingNotAvailable":"The purchase and pricing options for this item are unavailable. Select items are only available as part of a subscription package. You may try again later or <a href='https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/xpl/contact' target='_blank'>contact us</a> for more information."},"getProgramTermsAccepted":false,"sections":{"abstract":"true","authors":"true","figures":"true","multimedia":"false","references":"true","citedby":"false","keywords":"true","definitions":"false","algorithm":"false","dataset":"false","cadmore":"false","footnotes":"false","disclaimer":"false","relatedContent":"false","metrics":"true"},"graphicalAbstract":{"summary":"A novel network, named YOLO-CXR, is proposed for effectively locating multiple small lesions in chest X-ray images. Firstly, the proposed network enhances the YOLOv8s backbone by replacing the ordinary convolutional layers with RefConv layers to improve its feature extraction capabilities w.r.t. various diseases. Secondly, it utilizes a novel Efficient Channel and Local Attention (ECLA) mechanism to increase its sensitivity to the spatial location information of different lesions. Thirdly, to enhance its detection of small lesions, YOLO-CXR incorporates a dedicated small-lesion detection head and the Selective Feature Fusion (SFF) technique. Due to these improvements, the proposed network significantly enhances its detection of lesions at different scales and multiple small lesions in particular. Experiments conducted on the publicly available VinDr-CXR dataset demonstrate that YOLO-CXR achieves an mAP@0.5 of 0.338, a mAP@[0.5:0.95:0.05] of 0.167, and recall of 0.365, outperforming all state-of-the-art networks considered.","type":"graphic","fileSize":"92KB","file":"/ielx8/6287639/10380310/10720017/graphical_abstract/access-gagraphic-3482102.jpg","coverImage":"/ielx8/6287639/10380310/10720017/graphical_abstract/access-gagraphic-3482102.jpg"},"abstract":"Chest X-ray is one of the most widely used methods for clinical diagnosis of chest diseases. In recent years, the development of deep learning technologies has driven progress in chest disease detection, but existing methods still face numerous challenges. Current research primarily focuses on detecting specific chest diseases. However, when chest X-ray images indicate multiple diseases, the diverse and complex characteristics of different disease types make it challenging to extract effective information. Additionally, the detection accuracy of small lesions remains low, which lessens the overall lesion detection rate. To address these issues, a novel network, named YOLO-CXR, is proposed in this paper for multiple disease detection, which is able to effectively locate multiple small lesions in chest X-ray images. Firstly, the proposed network enhances the YOLOv8s backbone by replacing the ordinary convolutional layers with RefConv layers to improve its feature extraction capabilities w.r.t. various diseases. Secondly, it utilizes a novel Efficient Channel and Local Attention (ECLA) mechanism to increase its sensitivity to the spatial location information of different lesions. Thirdly, to enhance its detection of small lesions, YOLO-CXR incorporates a dedicated small-lesion detection head and the Selective Feature Fusion (SFF) technique. Due to these improvements, the proposed network significantly enhances its detection of lesions at different scales and multiple small lesions in particular. Experiments conducted on the publicly available VinDr-CXR dataset demonstrate that YOLO-CXR achieves an mAP@0.5 of 0.338, a mAP@[0.5:0.95:0.05] of 0.167, and recall of 0.365, outperforming all state-of-the-art networks considered.","publicationDate":"2024","publicationYear":"2024","pdfPath":"/iel8/6287639/10380310/10720017.pdf","doi":"10.1109/ACCESS.2024.3482102","displayPublicationTitle":"IEEE Access","formulaStrippedArticleTitle":"YOLO-CXR: A Novel Detection Network for Locating Multiple Small Lesions in Chest X-Ray Images","pdfUrl":"/stamp/stamp.jsp?tp=&arnumber=10720017","publicationTitle":"IEEE Access","startPage":"156003","endPage":"156019","keywords":[{"type":"IEEE Keywords","kwd":["Diseases","Lesions","Feature extraction","Accuracy","Lung","X-ray imaging","Location awareness","Solid modeling","Pneumonia","Medical diagnostic imaging","Biomedical image processing","Computer aided diagnosis"]},{"type":"Index Terms","kwd":["Chest X-ray","Small Lesions","Multiple Lesions","Lesion Images","Chest X-ray Images","Deep Learning","Detection Accuracy","Local Information","Convolutional Layers","Types Of Diseases","Spatial Information","Attention Mechanism","Disease Detection","Pulmonologists","Feature Fusion","Detection Of Lesions","Efficient Channel","Feature Extraction Capability","Detection Head","Local Attention","Convolutional Neural Network","Feature Maps","1D Convolution","Detection Model","Channel Attention","Bounding Box","Object Detection","Intersection Over Union Threshold","Training Loss","Convolution Kernel"]},{"type":"Author Keywords","kwd":["X-ray detection","image processing","computer aided diagnosis","object detection"]}],"doiLink":"https://doi.org/10.1109/ACCESS.2024.3482102","issueLink":"/xpl/tocresult.jsp?isnumber=10380310&punumber=6287639","authorNames":"Shengnan Hao;Xinlei Li;Wei Peng;Zhu Fan;Zhanlin Ji;Ivan Ganchev","allowComments":true,"pubLink":"/xpl/RecentIssue.jsp?punumber=6287639","displayPublicationDate":"16 October 2024","dateOfInsertion":"16 October 2024","isGetAddressInfoCaptured":false,"isMarketingOptIn":false,"pubTopics":[{"name":"Aerospace"},{"name":"Bioengineering"},{"name":"Communication, Networking and Broadcast Technologies"},{"name":"Components, Circuits, Devices and Systems"},{"name":"Computing and Processing"},{"name":"Engineered Materials, Dielectrics and Plasmas"},{"name":"Engineering Profession"},{"name":"Fields, Waves and Electromagnetics"},{"name":"General Topics for Engineers"},{"name":"Geoscience"},{"name":"Nuclear Engineering"},{"name":"Photonics and Electrooptics"},{"name":"Power, Energy and Industry Applications"},{"name":"Robotics and Control Systems"},{"name":"Signal Processing and Analysis"},{"name":"Transportation"}],"publisher":"IEEE","isEarlyAccess":false,"isOpenAccess":true,"isEphemera":false,"isConference":false,"displayDocTitle":"YOLO-CXR: A Novel Detection Network for Locating Multiple Small Lesions in Chest X-Ray Images","xploreDocumentType":"Journals & Magazine","isDynamicHtml":true,"isBookWithoutChapters":false,"isBook":false,"isChapter":false,"isProduct":false,"volume":"12","isSpringer":false,"isPromo":false,"isStandard":false,"isJournal":true,"isFreeDocument":true,"isOnlineOnly":false,"htmlAbstractLink":"/document/10720017/","isNow":false,"isLatestStandard":false,"isGiveaway":false,"hasStandardVersions":false,"isCustomDenial":false,"isTranslation":false,"isSAE":false,"isSMPTE":false,"persistentLink":"https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/servlet/opac?punumber=6287639","htmlLink":"/document/10720017/","isDegruyter":false,"isOUP":false,"startPage":"156003","fundingAgencies":{"fundingAgency":[{"fundingId":"10.13039/501100012166","fundingName":"National Key Research and Development Program of China","grantNumber":"2017YFE0135700"},{"fundingName":"Bulgarian National Science Fund (BNSF)","grantNumber":"KP-06-IP-CHINA/1"},{"fundingId":"10.13039/100007787","fundingName":"Telecommunications Research Centre (TRC), University of Limerick, Ireland"}]},"subjectCategories":["Computational and artificial intelligence","Computers and information processing"],"openAccessFlag":"T","insertDate":"16 October 2024","ephemeraFlag":"false","title":"YOLO-CXR: A Novel Detection Network for Locating Multiple Small Lesions in Chest X-Ray Images","html_flag":"false","ml_html_flag":"true","sourcePdf":"access-ganchev-3482102-x.pdf","displayPublicationDate":"16 October 2024","mlTime":"PT0.0736S","xplore-pub-id":"6287639","pdfPath":"/iel8/6287639/10380310/10720017.pdf","isNumber":"10380310","contentType":"periodicals","publicationDate":"2024","publicationNumber":"6287639","xplore-issue":"10380310","articleId":"10720017","publicationTitle":"IEEE Access","sections":{"abstract":"true","authors":"true","figures":"true","multimedia":"false","references":"true","citedby":"false","keywords":"true","definitions":"false","algorithm":"false","dataset":"false","cadmore":"false","footnotes":"false","disclaimer":"false","relatedContent":"false","metrics":"true"},"volume":"12","contentTypeDisplay":"Journals","referenceCount":57,"publicationYear":"2024","subType":"IEEE Journal","_value":"CCBY","lastupdate":"2025-03-09","mediaPath":"/mediastore/IEEE/content/media/6287639/10380310/10720017","endPage":"156019","displayPublicationTitle":"IEEE Access","doi":"10.1109/ACCESS.2024.3482102"};








